# Generated artifacts. Nothing here is reproducible from the source, and a
# stale one can shadow the source it was built from -- see
# tests/test_repo_hygiene.py for the incident that prompted this.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.egg-info/
# The READMEs tell people to build the environment at .venv/ inside the
# repository. Nothing ignored it, so `git status` offered a whole virtual
# environment as untracked -- and the language guard read its contents.
.venv/
venv/
# Per-method environments, one directory each, kept OUT of methods/ so that
# method-scanning tests never read a vendored package as the method's own
# source: test_method_requirements walks methods/<m> for *.py, and a venv there
# made it ast-parse the whole of torch. See docs/GPU.md section 2.
.venvs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Downloaded pretrained backbones (bin/fetch-weights.py). Large, pinned by
# sha256 in a method's provenance.json, and reproducible from there -- so the
# bytes are never tracked. The default --out lands here.
.weights/
